A||||43||Haagster||Who had to rush out and buy Windows XP?||||6||
Z||000000||Haagster||10-27-2001||09:23 AM||||I was just wondering how many of us are "geeks"?  Who bought into all of the Windows XP hype, and <B>HAD</B> to buy it on Thursday? <P>I for one, bought the Home version at 8:00 in the morning.  The woman behind the counter said that they'd already sold 100 of them since opening at 7:00AM.  I also had to go back (3 hours later) and buy a new modem, since mine wasn't compatible with NT/2K/XP...<p>[This message has been edited by Haagster (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||stimpy||10-27-2001||10:17 AM||||I was the first kid on the block with it, as the computer we bought 2 weeks ago was already loaded with it. Nanny nanna boo boo! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||10-27-2001||10:31 AM||||I will never understand why people insist on buying a product that has proven over the years to <B>not</B> work - only because there's a newer version of it. Most software companies will release bugfixes for what it is: a bugfix. Microsoft just calles it a <B>new</B> version, and charges you an arm and a leg for it - <B>and</B> gets away with it. Bill Gates must be laughing his a$$ off all the way to the bank.<P>I will <B>not</B> buy XP. Just as I did not buy into WinME (which was the previous latest and greatest, remember? And what a bunch of crap that turned out to be). I'll stick with Win98SE and if that turns out to be unsufficient to run the latest programs, I will throw out Windows completely and stick with Linux. There isn't anything you can do with Windows that you can't do with Linux better and faster anymore.<P>Oh well, enough of my ranting already. Go rush out and buy WinXP. Show the software world it isn't important anymore to have a finished, stable and mostly bugfree program <B>before</B> you sell it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Matthew_Fiero||10-27-2001||10:41 AM||||I have had no problems with windows me<BR>i hated win2k for its incompatibility but i loved it for its great features. I hated win98 for not having those features and win me brings them together. I only had problems the first few times installing it, when it was  so brand new it wasn't even out yet.<BR>Thanks<BR>Matthew||||reg||1
Z||000004||btoth||10-27-2001||11:59 AM||||I laughed my ass off when everyone waited outside all night in front of Bestbuy for Win98!!!!<P>I use Win2k.  I bought it a discount from my school.  There was no way I'd ever pay full price for any Microsoft product.  I mean... what are they charging for Office now???  It's rediculous.  And $1000 for Visual Studio? Gimmie a break.  All you use is C++ and VB, who uses the other programs that it comes with???<P>The only reason I have a PC is because of school and to play the occasional game.  Game companies should boycott Windows and develop for other platforms.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Then I'd just buy a new Mac with OS 10.1.<P>The best part about the Mac OS:  Programs install in their own folders, minus extentions and preferences.  You don't need stupid unistall programs just to delete a program and progams don't screw with your OS. (No stupid DLLs to screw up.)  The only things I never liked was the one menu bar and the fact that you actually have to quit programs from the menubar or else it just stays running in the background.  That, and Apple's computers are a rip-off.<P>Apple should port OS X directly to the PC and compete with Windows just for the heck of it.  It'd be funny.  I'd buy it.<P><p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||10-27-2001||12:28 PM||||I upgraded frm my old dual boot Windows NT/Win 98 setup and I really like it. The first thing I did after installing it was to get rid of the eye candy and trim back a bunch of the services, but it now is the quickest OS I have used. The memory footprint is pretty small; on bootup only 52 megs of memory are used, and I didn't have any problem with any of my hardware, in fact my old Vortex 2 soundcard that wouldn't work under NT now works with XP. I really like the multiple users now too. I have a huge games collection, and I have not had one game that will not run under XP. Also, all my CAD and 3d programs runwithout a hitch. Lastly, the smoothview fonts have to be seen to be believed, they look awesome. THe price is to high though in my opinion. For the upgrade to XP Pro from NT 4.0 the cost is $338. Yikes! ||||reg||1
Z||000006||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-27-2001||12:46 PM||||I am sticking with win98 first edition.<P>I actually once burned a copy of WINME, After a install, I formatted and threw the cd in the garbage..  I wasted a perfectly good cdr on this crap.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>I dont think anyone should buy win xp until they at least have the service pack 2 released..<P><BR>Heres my breakdown on OS's<BR>Win 3.1 & 3.11 Bill steals source code and compiles it and releases it<BR>Win95  M$'s first try @ 32 bit<BR>Win98  M$ tries to fix the bugs in 95  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>win98SE  M$ STILL tries to fix more "features"(we call them bugs) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Winme M$ removes a lot of extras that techs and powerusers liked about 98<BR>Win NT  pretty stable and with SP2, probably the most solid one..  still a lot of unsupported hardware<BR>WINXP M$ decided we needed even less control of our system then we had with Winme..<P><BR>My suggestion would be to test it before you buy it..even if you need to play on a store computer..<P><BR>PS <A HREF="http://www.lindows.com" TARGET=_blank>www.lindows.com</A>  will be releasing their OS later this year that will run LINUX & WIndows programs..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Haagster||10-27-2001||12:59 PM||||I bought (preordered) Windows 95 the day it was released.  Windows 98 got installed 2 days after it came out (never had SE).  Paid dearly for Windows 2000 Pro (even though everyone kept saying "Wait for Windows ME".  Bought the $50 for ME.  And now, spent another $100 on XP.  Yes, I am a geek (or idiot, or...).  Bill Gates has gotten more than his fair share of my son's inheritance.||||reg||6
Z||000008||Reality||10-27-2001||12:59 PM||||I have better things to spend $100.00 on ... Like my CAR!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haagster||10-27-2001||01:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR>Most software companies will release bugfixes for what it is: a bugfix. Microsoft just calles it a <B>new</B> version, and charges you an arm and a leg for it - <B>and</B> gets away with it. Bill Gates must be laughing his a$$ off all the way to the bank.<BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Remember the "release party" for Windows 95?  The computer crashed in the middle of Gate's speech - kudos to MS for that one.  The DAY Windows 2000 was released, there was a patch (and not a small one) that HAD to be downloaded to get it installed (at least on my stupid machine).  Millennium is still coming out with significant issues.  Cliff, you are absolutely right...<P>(I also have another computer running Mandrake, that I haven't had a problem with yet...)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||10-27-2001||04:10 PM||||I'm still trying to figure out some of the ME bugs.  (Don't ride me over this one.  It came on my computer and I didn't know I had a choice.)  I'll probably never get XP.  If Linux ever becomes compatible with all of the millions of Microsoft/Windows software out there, I'll probably try that.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Nashco||10-27-2001||04:49 PM||||I have Windows 2k, and I absolutely love it!  I don't have any USB stuff, so I don't have to worry about the lack of drivers.  I love it so much because it WILL NOT crash.  I've only ever had the computer freeze up once in over a year of abuse.  I also love the ability to monitor the system so easily by opening the task manager.<P>Oh, and why in the heck would you rush out and BUY XP?  You mean, people actually pay for windows products?  I can't believe it....no way....is that true?  I don't have any problem with windows, but I don't know anybody that's ever bought it.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000012||GTFiero1||10-27-2001||05:02 PM||||i have windows ME on both the computers because tehy came with it and im happy with them. i never noticed much difference between win95, 98 and ME . quite frankly i dont give a damn. they all have the same purpose and a new program that costs 100 buck for a cd and the only has tiny differences isnt worth it to me<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cliff Pennock||10-27-2001||05:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by isthiswhereiputausername?:<BR><B><A HREF="http://www.lindows.com" TARGET=_blank>www.lindows.com</A>  will be releasing their OS later this year that will run LINUX & WIndows programs..</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That shows you how powerful Linux is, because Lindows is actually Linux (core) with a Windows emulator.||||reg||1
Z||000014||grinthock||10-27-2001||06:02 PM||||I am running the released verison of XP PRo at home, no major changes really, it's the same old OS as windows 2000 really, a couple major MAJOR kernel upgrades and changed, memory management is WAY BETTER (doesn't lock up the ram as much)<P>There are a couple quirky things that bug me like how all of a sudden it just STOPS for about 5 seconds (stops EVERYTHING) and then comes back, but I was running it for 7 days STRAIGHT with no reboots and it was still flying around.<P>You can even install software and most drivers without rebooting now (sounds like crashintosh!)<P><BR>My opinion?  Unless you are a super mega geek like me, don't bother upgrading till at LEAST service Pack 1 is released a month from now.<P><BR>Oh, and Office XP is cool.<P><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Loki||10-27-2001||06:09 PM||||Well I didnt run out an buy it, but I did d/l it about a month ago   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Full blown corp version..Not bad. But still using ME<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/loki_sig.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/w4[1].gif"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
