Z||000029||Spektrum-87GT||10-28-2001||05:34 PM||||microsoft is watching<P>i've heard they can monitor everything you do when connected to the internet. like they have they're own little backdoor. i think i'll stick with win2k pro, because its by far the best operating system i've ever used(i started back in the days of ms-dos v3.0 and have used unix/x windows, macos, etc. in college) I've had it lock up on me once and it wasnt windows fault... i dont think||||reg||1
Z||000030||banditbalz||10-28-2001||05:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>i think i'll stick with win2k pro, because its by far the best operating system i've ever used(i started back in the days of ms-dos v3.0 and have used unix/x windows, macos, etc. in college) I've had it lock up on me once and it wasnt windows fault... i dont think</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Iv'e been running Win 2000 Pro for a week now and it has locked up on me twice. Also, the OS does not recognize my sound card, video card or my 3D accelerator (3DFX). Was actually prepaired to upgrade to Win XP Pro today... just  couldn't see dropping another $149 on a OS with no recognizable drivers!<P>Linux is looking better all the time!<P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||13
