ns<BR>VME bus: adapter 13<BR>VME bus: adapter 0 mapped to adapter 13<BR>EPC external interrupts<BR>colour//home &gt; <P><BR>||||reg||3
Z||000035||Hippocrat||10-29-2001||03:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>I will never understand why people insist on buying a product that has proven over the years to [b]not</B> work - only because there's a newer version of it. Most software companies will release bugfixes for what it is: a bugfix. Microsoft just calles it a <B>new</B> version, and charges you an arm and a leg for it - <B>and</B> gets away with it. Bill Gates must be laughing his a$$ off all the way to the bank.<P>B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry to correct you here Cliff.. <P>After reading your post, I called Microsoft and confirmed what I thought. These are not bugs in the software they are referred to as "FEATURES"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Only the rest of the world the ones who have been privileged enough to use a real OS (Linux, BSD etc.) call them bugs. <P>NO XPU FOR ME EITHER. <P>I do however almost somewhat kinda like 200pro  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000036||btoth||10-29-2001||09:44 AM||||For the most part I like Win2k Pro.  (As far as Windows goes.)  There are things about it that are a bit of a pain... like the no ASPI drivers, a lot of my CD-ROM software only supports ASPI.  No biggie, I found a place that has all the latest WinNT drivers.  Voodoo4... can't just do the straight forward install, because it wants to use the Win98 installers, which is a no-no.  No biggie, install it manually.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  Couple games won't work.  No big deal.  The ones I actually like, and most new games can run under Win2k just fine.  And if they crash... and you know they do... Win2k doesn't give a s#$%.  Even when explorer crashes... and it does quite often (still), it doesn't bring the rest of the computer down with it.<P>I'm not trying to sell anyone on it... please avoid Microsoft at all costs...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  but sometimes if you want stability, you have to sacrafice compatability.<P>Unfortunatly, the software companies only focus on Windows (except for a small %).  I always said, when I owned my Macs, that if the game companies shifted to the Mac side, people would buy Macs.  Games where the only thing I couldn't do with my Mac.  I still think, Apple should focus on the software and let others develop the hardware.  I want to be CEO of that company  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'd turn it around!||||reg||1
Z||000037||btoth||10-29-2001||09:46 AM||||I did download Darwin.  Very cool to see my PC say 'Welcome to Macintosh'.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Now if someone would just develope a kick-@$$ GUI that mimicks the Aqua interface, that'd be cool.||||reg||1
Z||000038||JSocha||10-29-2001||11:12 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> Lets see:<P>Windows 98SE2 (+ Patches)  Unstable, crashes, General Faults.<P>Windows NT Workstation/Server w/sp6 - More stable but loose features of right clicking and occasional CORE DUMPS.<P>Windows 2000 Pro - More stable, fewer to no crashes, less General Protection Faults, features of NT & 98, little harder to apply settings, but liveable, drivers harder to find to run older components or no driver upgrades available.<P>Windows XP - Definate Memory and processor hog.  Requires more memory to run, requires a faster processor.  So if you ain't running a GIGAHERZ system, your screwed.<P>Order I would look at it:<BR>Windows 98se2 (Just live with the crashes)<P>Windows NT Workstation and/or Server with Service Patch 6<P>Windows 2000 PRO providing I know that drivers for my older devices were available or software patches from 3rd party application developers have provided 2K compatability patches.<P>Windows XP - Only if I have a CRAY styled computer system sitting in my basement at an affordable price.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000039||Master_Sushi||10-29-2001||12:15 PM||||BUY? HA! Real geeks won't do that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">!<P>I stoped "upgrading" when win98SE came out. It seems to work fine for me. I have winME, but I only run it on one of my computers. I use to be a softwareZ nut, but it got kind of boring after a while and I gave up on it. It was kind of fun though. It was mostly for braging rights. Like... "I have every version of office and windows ever made, they are indexed in my 30 page cd binder" hehe.<P>Anyways, once Linux gets a little bit more compatable im going to switch over to it. I probably could switch to it now but im lazy. Dumping *microflop winslow* will be a great thing!!!||||reg||10
Z||000040||Tigger||10-29-2001||12:18 PM||||So has anyone got a blue screen error running XP???  I just gotta know.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Ohhh yea, about Internet Explorer crashing and taking the entire system down with it, mine does it a lot.  After downloading the latest service pack for IE which it now gives me a warning before it crashes.<P>It's kinda like that red oil warning light on the dash that turns on a second before the engine grenades.<P>I think Windows95 with Fat32 and more plug-n-play than Windows 3.1 seemed to be the best (well sorta) step forward.  I wasn't impressed with Win98, just a few changes here and there, drop it in the box, create a new logo, cover it with shrink wrap, and put it on the shelves.  I watched a lot of friends waste a ton of time trying to get it to work right when it first came out and lost a lot of respect for MS then.<P>Whatever you do don't buy the "Upgrade packs" from one version to the next version.  My friend tried that I think between Win95 to Wind98 and it did nothing but screw things up after installing it.  After wasting a bunch of time he finally broke down and bought the full version then it work "better".<P>Windows OS to me really are not that bad.  It just I don't expect to have to shut off and restart a brand new car because it develops unexplained intermittent misses all the time. <P>Finally, has anyone notice when you try to view the "new" MSN webpage (redesigned for the release of XP), it crashes and bombs out Netscape completely when the background is that dark blue and nothing has loaded yet.<P>Hmmm...  makes ya wonder?        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-29-2001).]||||reg||1
